    "Low Medium High. A measure of the extent to which a user is willing to accept uncertainty and potential adverse outcomes related to climate risks. For example, a low risk tolerance indicates a preference for detailed quantification of even the most extreme climate scenarios, enabling proactive planning and adaptation to minimise potential impacts. ": 1,
    "The task of analysing and projecting the future climate by creating an output metric based on the selected climate simulations.": 1,
